icitly instead of CO2 alone\",\n        \"Specify concentrated drying or evaporitic conditions for rxn_009\",\n        \"Rewrite rxn_011 as mol_011 + 2 mol_001 -> mol_009 + mol_003 + mol_010\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.72,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.42,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.7\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.58,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.56,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.38,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.84,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.59,\n      \"feedback\": \"The detour through hydantoin is the main problem. rxn_010, carboxylative cyclization of glycinamide to hydantoin from CO2 alone, is under-justified and likely needs a more activated carbamylating chemistry or much tighter condition control. The pathway also depends on the poorly specified biochemical environment used in rxn_006 and on stoichiometric correction of rxn_011.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_006\",\n        \"rxn_010\",\n        \"rxn_011\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Do not use rxn_010 without an explicit activating agent or stronger mechanistic justification\",\n        \"Relabel rxn_006 to a prebiotically plausible aqueous or hydrothermal setting\",\n        \"Rewrite rxn_011 with 2 H2O and specify harsh hydrolysis conditions if this detour is retained\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.82,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.88,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.72,\n        \"rxn_010\": 0.42,\n        \"rxn_011\": 0.7\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.6,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.58,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.37,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.84,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.6,\n      \"feedback\": \"Although the early Strecker chemistry is reasonable, the pathway becomes weak once it diver